leds: pmi8950-torch: optional "label" for the LED name

Applies on top of 0014 (the torch driver from postmarketos-xiaomi-vince). The
driver always named the LED "white:torch"; Phosh's torch toggle looks for
"*:flash". Read an optional DT "label" (kernel/dts/...-torch.dtsi sets
"white:flash"), so the name can differ per device without changing the default.

Signed-off-by: Dimitris Vagiakakos <dimitrislinuxos@protonmail.ch>

--- a/drivers/leds/leds-qcom-pmi8950-torch.c
+++ b/drivers/leds/leds-qcom-pmi8950-torch.c
@@ -682,7 +682,9 @@
 	torch->mc_cdev.num_colors = PMI8950_TORCH_CHANNELS;
 	torch->mc_cdev.subled_info = torch->subled;
 	cdev = &torch->mc_cdev.led_cdev;
+	/* Optional DT "label": e.g. "white:flash" is what Phosh's torch toggle looks for. */
 	cdev->name = "white:torch";
+	device_property_read_string(dev, "label", &cdev->name);
 	cdev->brightness = LED_OFF;
 	cdev->max_brightness = PMI8950_TORCH_MAX_BRIGHTNESS;
 	cdev->color = LED_COLOR_ID_WHITE;
